          "entradaId": "freeman-532",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "Peer, “beauty,” is the same word that is rendered “bonnet” in Isaiah 3:20 where see the note (#486). The prophet wishes to allow the contrast between the time of mourning and that of rejoicing. The mourner sits with ashes on the head. See note on 2 Samuel 15:32 (#279). When the m…",
        "traduccion": {
          "resourceId": "freeman-532",
          "sourceHash": "678f029895b47721a1bbfbdfd872a959acfb655cb399078969af416537c846b1",
          "sourceLanguage": "en"
        }
      },
      "c-8c1adc79a9029527": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-533",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "At Oriental weddings both bride and bridegroom are adorned with a profusion of jewelry of every kind. If too poor to purchase they borrow from neighbors and friends, that a splendid show may be made. See also Revelation 21:2.",
        "traduccion": {
          "resourceId": "freeman-533",
          "sourceHash": "b70ea1ea796cad93eef4145807c70de5106e4717d183a8a33cdb47b8005ec92f",
          "sourceLanguage": "en"
        }
      }
